From 0af512d79c0fc61c007051f522ba617be6836535 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:06:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm: TF_GLM_SLOT_RESUME, a later prompt resumes on its slot's
 own prompt rows

A prompt pass on glm_moe_dsa starts where the rows the slot's last prompt pass left stand for the new prompt: the
longest common token prefix, cut back to a chunk start of that pass on the 4,096-row grid (every chunk before it
whole and alone), at least one row (beside a drafter, DFlash2's whole window) short of the new prompt's end, under
the same request policy mask and with no other begin on the slot since. Nothing is copied and no memory is set
aside: the latent rows (int8 codes and both scale planes), the DSA index keys (rings spanning the capacity) and the
pooled keys are positional, and rows past the point are rewritten before they are read, as after State.reset. The
drafter restarts from 0 as a fresh pass's does and re-taps its window. Every rank agrees (Engine.rewind, one
all-reduce) or none moves and the pass starts at 0. KV pages, KV shard, image prompts, prompt logprobs, the target
MTP head without a drafter and batched prompt passes do not resume. TF_GLM_KV_SPLIT keeps its positional layout
(position p on rank p mod W), so a split sequence resumes the same way.

The resumed rows count as cached: the done line's cached= and usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens.
Default on; TF_GLM_SLOT_RESUME=0 turns it off. The idea is TensorFold's Metal qwen27 slot resume
(native/qwen27_resume.zig, TF_QWEN27_SLOT_RESUME); this is a new implementation for the CUDA GLM path.

Host tests: zig build test-glm-slot-resume-host (6 named tests).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQVvNktFCvQrvpNUbqtqBX
